hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1399.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zaynab bint Abi Salama from Umm Salama
1399.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zaynab bint Abi Salama from Umm Salama
1400.1,Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab had a dispute brought to him between a muslim and a jew. Umar saw that the right belonged to the jew and decided in his favour. The jew said to him
1400.2,Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab had a dispute brought to him between a muslim and a jew. Umar saw that the right belonged to the jew and decided in his favour. The jew said to him
1401.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Abu Amra al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah
1401.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Abu Amra al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah
1402.1,
1402.2,"Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Muhammad
Sirin used to say, ""Do not sell grain on the ears until it is white.""


Malik said, ""If someone buys food for a known price to be
delivered at a stated date, and when the date comes, the one who owes
the food says, 'I do not have any food, sell me the food which I owe
you with delayed terms.' The owner of the food says, 'This is not
good, because the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant
him peace, forbade selling food until the deal was completed.' The one
who owes the food says to his creditor, 'Sell me any kind of food on
delayed terms until I discharge the debt to you.' This is not good
because he gives him food and then he returns it to him. The gold
which he gave him becomes the price of that which is his right against
him and the food which he gave him becomes what clears what is between
them. If they do that, it becomes the sale of food before the deal is
complete.""


Malik spoke about a man who was owed food which he
had purchased from a man and this man was owed the like of that food
by another man. The one who owed the food said to his creditor, ""I
will refer you to my debtor who owes me the same amount of food as I
owe you, so that you may obtain the food which I owe you .""


Malik said, ""If the man who had to deliver the food, had gone out, and
bought the food to pay off his creditor, that is not good. That is
selling food before taking possession of it. If the food is an advance
which falls due at that particular time, there is no harm in paying
off his creditor with it because that is nota sale. It is not halal to
sell food before receiving it in full since the Messenger of Allah,
may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade that. However, the
people of knowledge agree that there is no harm in partnership,
transfer of responsibility and revocation in sales of food and other
goods.""


Malik said, ""That is because the people of knowledge
consider it as a favour rendered. They do not consider it as a sale.
It is like a man lending light dirhams. He is then paid back in
dirhams of full weight, and so gets back more than he lent. That is
halal for him and permitted. Had a man bought defective dirhams from
him as being the full weight, that would not be halal. Had it been
stipulated to him that he lend full weight in dirhams, and then he
gave faulty ones, that would not be halal for him."""
1403.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzalah."
1403.2,"Yahya related to me from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzalah ibn Qays al-Zurayqi, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the renting of farmland. Hanzalah said: \So I asked Rafi' ibn Khadij", 'What about with gold and silver?' He said: 'As for with gold and silver," there is no harm in it.'\"""""
1404.1,Yahya said from Malik that he heard from Sulayman ibn Yasar and others that when they were asked whether the testimony of a man flogged for a hadd crime was permitted
1404.2,Yahya said from Malik that he heard from Sulayman ibn Yasar and others that when they were asked whether the testimony of a man flogged for a hadd crime was permitted
1405.1,"And Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Yunus bin Yusuf, from Sa'id bin Al-Musayyab, that Umar bin Al-Khattab passed by Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah while he was selling his raisins in the market. Umar bin Al-Khattab said to him: \Either you increase the price"," or you remove yourself from our market.\"""""
1405.2,"And Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he asked Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar about renting out farms. He said: \There is no harm in it for gold and silver.\"" Ibn Shihab said: \""So I said to him: What do you think about the hadith that is mentioned from Rafi' bin Khadij?\"" He said: \""Rafi' exaggerated. If I had a farm"," I would rent it out.\"""""
