1416.1,"And Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer. Meaning by the dowry of a prostitute what a woman is given for fornication, and the fee of a soothsayer is his bribe and what is given for soothsaying."
1416.2,"And Malik narrated to me that it reached him that Umar bin Al-Khattab said: \The testimony of an opponent or someone suspected is not permissible.\"""""
1417.1,Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari that his father said
1417.2,Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari that his father said
