1446.2,Malik related to me from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Yazid
1447.1,Malik related to me from Ayyub ibn Musa from Muawiya ibn Abdullah ibn Badr al-Juhani that his father informed him that he stopped with a people on the way to Syria and he found a purse which had eighty dinars in it. He mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said to him
1447.2,Malik related to me from Ayyub ibn Musa from Muawiya ibn Abdullah ibn Badr al-Juhani that his father informed him that he stopped with a people on the way to Syria and he found a purse which had eighty dinars in it. He mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said to him
1448.1,Malik related to me from Nafi that a man found something and went to Abdullah ibn Umar and said to him
1448.2,Malik related to me from Nafi that a man found something and went to Abdullah ibn Umar and said to him
1449.1,"Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he asked him about a man who rents a beast of burden and then rents it out for more than he rented it for. He said: \There is no harm in that.\"""""
1449.2,"Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Thurayh bin Zayd al-Dili, that he said: It has reached me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Any house or land that was divided in the Jahiliyyah", then it is according to the division of the Jahiliyyah. And any house or land that Islam reached and it was not divided," then it is according to the division of Islam.\"""""
1450.1,Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said while he was leaning his back against the Kaba
1450.2,Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said while he was leaning his back against the Kaba
1451.1,"Malik narrated to me, from al-Ala' bin Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from his grandfather, that Uthman bin Affan gave him wealth as a qirad (a type of partnership) to work with, on the condition that the profit would be between them."
1451.2,"Malik narrated to me, from Hisham bin Urwah, from his father, from Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman bin Hatib, that some slaves of Hatib stole a she-camel belonging to a man from Muzaynah. They slaughtered it. This was brought to Umar bin al-Khattab, and Umar ordered Kathir bin al-Salt to cut off their hands. Then Umar said: \I think you are starving them.\"" Then Umar said: \""By Allah"," I will make you pay a fine that will be difficult for you.\"" Then he said to the Muzani: \""What was the price of your she-camel?\"" The Muzani said: \""By Allah"," I used to prevent it from being sold for less than four hundred dirhams.\"" Umar said: \""Give him eight hundred dirhams.\"""""
1452.1,Malik related to me from Said ibn Amr Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubada from his father that his father said
1452.2,Malik related to me from Said ibn Amr Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubada from his father that his father said
1453.1,Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha
1453.2,"Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that she said: ""Abu Bakr as-Siddiq had given her twenty wasqs of his property from al-Ghaba as a gift. When his death approached, he said, 'By Allah, my daughter, there is no one among the people after me I would prefer to see wealthy than you, and no one I would be more distressed to see poor. I gave you twenty wasqs as a gift. If you had harvested and taken possession of it, it would have been yours. Today, however, it is the property of the heirs. Your two brothers and your two sisters are the heirs. So divide it according to the Book of Allah"
1454.1,Malik related to me that he heard that a man of the Ansar from the tribe of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj
1454.2,Malik related to me that he heard that a man of the Ansar from the tribe of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj
